                    {
                        "sense_id": "708653f8-1e8c-399c-8745-3a0662e9008b",
                        "entry_id": "6381a425-753b-38f9-b734-ba0d13fcee60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Würfel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "regional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bdf00b5-83ae-48dd-a030-6dd033b39e2d",
                                "sense_id": "708653f8-1e8c-399c-8745-3a0662e9008b",
                                "text": "Die Kinder spielten mit den Knobeln."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18f22d56-3515-4da1-aae9-dac8462e43b3",
                        "source_entry_id": "6381a425-753b-38f9-b734-ba0d13fcee60",
                        "source_sense_id": "708653f8-1e8c-399c-8745-3a0662e9008b",
                        "source_sense_description": "Würfel",
                        "target_lang_word": "dice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8f695bb-295c-3a74-abd5-9d79df4d8833",
                                        "entry_id": "a2137a58-b916-3307-901f-114b31fe4137",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gaming with one or more dice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d568c2b4-52eb-43d7-84db-a79b97700e39",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f695bb-295c-3a74-abd5-9d79df4d8833",
                                                "text": "Or think of a decent young citizen in a toga—perhaps too much dice, you know—coming out here in the train of some prefect, or tax-gatherer, or trader even, to mend his fortunes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5e9aee4-66f8-4654-9c27-34824d962064",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f695bb-295c-3a74-abd5-9d79df4d8833",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, evolution is not a matter of chance, even in the sense in which a game of dice is a game of chance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fb193c0-addc-40fd-8a9c-6d707814ad71",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f695bb-295c-3a74-abd5-9d79df4d8833",
                                                "text": "I, at any rate, am convinced that He is not playing at dice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a5b5128-037e-4658-9710-3d9dd2dfe37c",
                                                "sense_id": "f8f695bb-295c-3a74-abd5-9d79df4d8833",
                                                "text": "The problem is that no one can throw a die twice in precisely the same way, and this is why dice is a game of chance and not a skill."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fd5cdac-9303-333d-b9eb-a2ef61bc6d39",
                                        "entry_id": "a2137a58-b916-3307-901f-114b31fe4137",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A die."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45b608e7-a660-4de3-a74a-acc0184d103c",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd5cdac-9303-333d-b9eb-a2ef61bc6d39",
                                                "text": "1980, Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus, “The Winner Takes It All”, Super Trouper, Polar Music\nThe gods may throw a dice / Their minds as cold as ice"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7f4e375-8ca4-4736-85a0-d458662fe8c3",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd5cdac-9303-333d-b9eb-a2ef61bc6d39",
                                                "text": "A white house set like a dice on a rock already venerable with the scars of wind and water."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19977935-1362-4cfc-b030-1b20a455ba42",
                                                "sense_id": "3fd5cdac-9303-333d-b9eb-a2ef61bc6d39",
                                                "text": "When we see a dice, we see an object which has six sides, some of which can be seen from where we are, others can be seen if we twist it or move around it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "378c8fbf-c0d0-3644-aded-d57347e39566",
                                        "entry_id": "a2137a58-b916-3307-901f-114b31fe4137",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which has been diced."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9a07fcb-9b09-4edf-9721-01c4a931d34f",
                                                "sense_id": "378c8fbf-c0d0-3644-aded-d57347e39566",
                                                "text": "Cut onions, carrots and celery into medium dice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ef36559-4efe-470e-b104-a0aded8911a7",
                                                "sense_id": "378c8fbf-c0d0-3644-aded-d57347e39566",
                                                "text": "If your worship is inclined to take a small draught of good wine, though not very cool, I have here a calabash full of the best, and some dices of Tronchon cheese"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f401fd57-38b4-3095-baf5-5927ff2acf95",
                                        "entry_id": "77f09708-b176-3e92-b799-4e29bcaed788",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "plural of die"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d092bd3-d7fe-3c13-ac6c-459681f8e203",
                                        "entry_id": "06cda9f5-0a38-387b-abc8-ad09e20e3435",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play dice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd67f571-f33d-42a2-a757-b2a289346a1c",
                                                "sense_id": "1d092bd3-d7fe-3c13-ac6c-459681f8e203",
                                                "text": "Virtuous enough; swore little; diced not above seven times — a week"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90a4ca43-4bdd-4839-95cc-1c49e7762028",
                                                "sense_id": "1d092bd3-d7fe-3c13-ac6c-459681f8e203",
                                                "text": "For Corinius, who gave not a fig for music or dirges, but liked well of carding and dicing, had brought forth his dice box to play with the son of Corund."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "055d0ec0-25b7-42d5-858a-93fa155bf7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "1d092bd3-d7fe-3c13-ac6c-459681f8e203",
                                                "text": "Tyrion found Timmett dicing with his Burned Men in the barracks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09134f4a-d50f-3ff1-abea-b728dc230b72",
                                        "entry_id": "06cda9f5-0a38-387b-abc8-ad09e20e3435",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut into small cubes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce40ea17-9050-4e46-aba0-5592c8551c48",
                                                "sense_id": "09134f4a-d50f-3ff1-abea-b728dc230b72",
                                                "text": "And dicing Time for gladness casts a moan...."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89927434-cdf4-42b1-a0ad-7505d4e3b88f",
                                                "sense_id": "09134f4a-d50f-3ff1-abea-b728dc230b72",
                                                "text": "Dice the vegetables and heat in the double boiler with butter, pepper and salt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4e09e38-5aa2-491c-b514-1456a52471aa",
                                                "sense_id": "09134f4a-d50f-3ff1-abea-b728dc230b72",
                                                "text": "But as our urban lives have grown more pressed for time, we have diced our opportunity costs finer and finer; from budgeting days or slabs of hours, we have come to rationing minutes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45d16971-1546-3a12-a908-a88676c1b633",
                                        "entry_id": "06cda9f5-0a38-387b-abc8-ad09e20e3435",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To ornament with squares, diamonds, or cubes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3ca70980-8a15-40d6-bf3e-c057f2e3dfbc",
                        "source_entry_id": "6381a425-753b-38f9-b734-ba0d13fcee60",
                        "source_sense_id": "708653f8-1e8c-399c-8745-3a0662e9008b",
                        "source_sense_description": "Würfel",
                        "target_lang_word": "dé",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18fd62a6-81d9-33cd-b0e5-df2a39fd233a",
                                        "entry_id": "b74ddf2a-089a-37d9-8999-77eca0dce59b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Objet cylindrique dans lequel on peut insérer un doigt pour le protéger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f01baf-c062-4fac-bc1d-eb315f99e8cb",
                                                "sense_id": "18fd62a6-81d9-33cd-b0e5-df2a39fd233a",
                                                "text": "Ma tante, voici le dé de ma mère, je le gardais précieusement dans ma toilette de voyage, dit Charles en présentant un joli dé d’or à madame Grandet, qui depuis dix ans en désirait un,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4216c82-01db-4e38-8116-37358e2724a9",
                                                "sense_id": "18fd62a6-81d9-33cd-b0e5-df2a39fd233a",
                                                "text": "– Je n’ai pas une croûte de pain, pas un os. – Et de la choucroute ? – Pas de quoi mettre dans le dé de ma femme !"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1d263dc-2327-4aaa-9d74-b34b38b54098",
                                                "sense_id": "18fd62a6-81d9-33cd-b0e5-df2a39fd233a",
                                                "text": "— Je ne vous en veux plus d’être venue, dit-elle enfin ; et fouillant dans un coffret de bois dur : « je voudrais que vous emportiez un souvenir de cette visite, que vous n’aurez peut-être pas l’occasion de renouveler. Voici un mauvais petit dé d’argent, mais qui a été mon premier. Prenez-le, et si jamais il vous arrivait quelque chose de grave où je puisse vous servir, envoyez-le moi avec votre adresse et quelqu’un passera chez vous de ma part. »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cc88ffc-d445-45e8-a651-f2a4f836165f",
                                                "sense_id": "18fd62a6-81d9-33cd-b0e5-df2a39fd233a",
                                                "text": "Une des couturières lui apprit l’air et chantonnait avec lui, tirant ses bas qui tombaient et son sarrau qui remontait ; il s’en alla après les avoir embrassées toutes, même la fille Renaud qui n’avait ni cils ni sourcils, et il n’eut pas la malice de mêler leurs dés."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6af6d82-fb1d-3380-a9c1-b01287b76b90",
                                        "entry_id": "5c8c35e5-d7be-3b6b-912b-f753c6567a43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit polyèdre, souvent cubique, autrefois d’os ou d’ivoire et de nos jours de bois ou de plastique, dont chacune des faces est marquée d’un nombre, qui est souvent représenté sous forme de creux ou de tâches, ou d’un symbole et qui sert à jouer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d05598b1-388d-4099-ae7d-7722b6980a04",
                                                "sense_id": "f6af6d82-fb1d-3380-a9c1-b01287b76b90",
                                                "text": "Mais par-dessus tout il avait l’indécision en horreur, et gardait depuis nombre d’années, comme un fétiche, le dé d’un jeu de tric-trac que dans le temps lui avait donné Baldi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df06a0dd-27f4-4bca-9ef9-178d23bedf5f",
                                                "sense_id": "f6af6d82-fb1d-3380-a9c1-b01287b76b90",
                                                "text": "Sa spécialité consistait à scier les dés et à les piper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5961771-b5b5-42aa-81c3-7ca76ef86d1a",
                                                "sense_id": "f6af6d82-fb1d-3380-a9c1-b01287b76b90",
                                                "text": "– Qu'est-ce que vous vouliez écouter ? lui demanda le patron en jetant sur le velours vert de la piste les trois dés qu'il avait dans la main. — (Lorris Murail, Bleu cerise, Gründ, 2010)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b68bc4f7-9e7b-356c-b3d9-4112405cf49a",
                                        "entry_id": "5c8c35e5-d7be-3b6b-912b-f753c6567a43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Objet dont la forme cubique rappelle celle d’un dé à jouer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a20ffb32-65fe-4d70-b17e-23b697860736",
                                                "sense_id": "b68bc4f7-9e7b-356c-b3d9-4112405cf49a",
                                                "text": "Couper de la viande en dés."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96eaf545-3b46-3871-b762-cee9ee8e9437",
                                        "entry_id": "5c8c35e5-d7be-3b6b-912b-f753c6567a43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tout autre objet aux faces numérotées, permettant de faire un jet aléatoire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80f6a998-4f1b-44d3-b4a7-9f200fbe7cb4",
                                                "sense_id": "96eaf545-3b46-3871-b762-cee9ee8e9437",
                                                "text": "Il existe des dés à quatre, huit, dix, douze, vingt, voire même trente faces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dé",
